※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4632

※ A place reached through a reference parameter is the caller's, and what is
※ written there is read after the call has ended.  A lambda the call was handed
※ lasts only as long as the call, as far as the call can tell, so it may not be
※ put there; one the call writes itself may, its environment then being kept
※ in `⎕heap`.

type Box = f: fn(u8) → u8

@[impure]
fn keep(b: &mut Box, g: fn(u8) → u8):
    b⌖.f ← g

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
